        <Row>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">#VTN_PoI_hatch</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">呃锁上了。</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">Untranslatable joke. (Reference to John Locke and the hatch in "Lost".) Can be translated with the generic/literal "it's locked".  It’s a locked hatch or door. All doors in the game are locked; it’s a running joke.</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">It's Locke'd.</Data>
          </Cell>
        </Row>
        <Row>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">#VTN_PoI_stuckaround</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">这只哥布林似乎被卡住了。</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">Reference to Arnold's one-liner in "Predator". (Schwartzennegger tells his enemy to "stick around" when he's impaled on a tree.) The goblin is stuck to a tree.</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">Looks like this goblin stuck around.</Data>
          </Cell>
        </Row>
        <Row>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">#VTN_PoI_mortars</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">一些迫击炮。都湿透了，&#10;散发着难闻的尿味。</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">Reference to the film "We Were Soldiers" where they urinate on the mortars to cool them off.</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">Some mortar equipment. They're all wet and a foul odor is emanating from them.</Data>
          </Cell>
        </Row>
        <Row>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">#VTN_PoI_mowgli</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">哦可怜的家伙，被蚂蚁吃光光啦。</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">In the Disney movie The Junglebook, the bear Baloue(?) teaches the kid Mowgli to find and eat ants from under rocks.  In the game, there's a big boulder with a pair of legs with red shorts sticking out from under it. The player sees the ants when examining the location.</Data>
          </Cell>
          <Cell>
            <Data ss:Type="String">Poor guy. There's ants swarming all over him.</Data>
          </Cell>
        </Row>
      </Table>
    </Worksheet>
